# Runtime output and local configuration; not part of the artefact.
#
# Every path is anchored with a leading `/` or is a directory name. A bare
# `config.yaml` reads as "any file with that name at any depth", which is not
# what this file means: 454 of the published runs carry their own `config.yaml`
# — the record of what that run was configured to do, and the only place the
# artefact states the model, the prompt language and the solver budget the
# batch ran under. An unanchored rule silently kept every one of them out of
# the repository while the release itself reported success.

# The two configurations a person fills in. Both hold an API key.
/config.yaml
/experiments/config.yaml

# Where the pipeline writes when someone runs it here.
/reproduced/
/a_runs/
/a_batches/
/work_results/

# Editor and interpreter leavings.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.idea/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
